    "chunk_text": "1. Supply of Services through an Electronic Platform\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'07'01Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 01.07.20252A\n\nNote: Even if a service is not listed above, it may still be subject to VAT if it falls within the scope described under item 1.1\n\n2. VAT Registration Requirements\n\n2.1. Before registering with VAT, Non-resident person requires to obtain a Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN) 2.2. Obtaining TIN and VAT Registration can be done through the e-service (use IRD\u2019s web portal www.ird.gov.lk). 2.3. A non - resident person who supplies services through an electronic platform to consumers in Sri Lanka must register for VAT, if the value of services supplied exceeds the threshold of Rs. 60,000,000 (Sixty Million Sri Lankan Rupees) within the last twelve months, or Rs. 15,000,000 (Fifteen Million Sri Lankan Rupees) within the last three months, as stipulated by the VAT Act. 2.4. Non-resident persons are responsible for collecting and remiting the VAT on their supply of services through an electronic platform not later than the twentieth day of the month following the end of the taxable period. 2.5. Non-resident persons should file VAT returns not later than the last day of the month after expiry of each taxable period (Quarterly basis).\n\n3. Registration Certificate"
